/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  cstr02_reversible_wgs  --  water-gas-shift reaction in a CSTR with
                             reverse rate from thermodynamic K_eq.

  Feed: equimolar CO + H2O at 600 K, 10 bar.  The forward Arrhenius
  kinetics drives a high conversion in the early residence times;
  the reverse term (auto-derived from g_pure_ig of the four species
  at T = 600 K) caps the conversion at the Le Chatelier equilibrium.

  At T = 600 K (the run prints Kp(T) from the same g_pure_ig):
      dG_rxn  =  g_CO2 + g_H2 - g_CO - g_H2O   ≈  -16.65 kJ/mol
      K_eq    =  exp(16650 / (R · 600))        ≈  28.2
      For equimolar CO + H2O (sum nu = 0, so Kc = Kp),
      K_eq = X^2 / (1-X)^2  -->  X_eq = sqrt(K)/(1 + sqrt(K)) ≈ 0.841

  THE FEED IS A GAS, AND THE SPACE TIME IS THE GAS'S.  The cstr reads the
  feed's phase at its own (T, P, z) -- all vapour here -- and takes the
  volumetric flow from the case's equation of state (ideal gas):
      Q   = F R T / P = (1/3.6 mol/s)(8.314)(600)/(1e6) ≈ 1.386e-3 m^3/s
      C0  = P / (2 R T) ≈ 100.2 mol/m^3 of each reactant
      tau = V_R / Q   ≈ 7.22 s   for V_R = 1e-2 m^3
  The design equation  X = k tau C0 [(1-X)^2 - X^2/K]  with k tau C0 ≈ 785
  puts X about 0.003 below X_eq: the conversion approaches (but does not
  exceed) the thermodynamic ceiling, X ≈ 0.839 against 0.841.  (Until
  2026-11-13 the unit priced this gas on its components' 25 C LIQUID
  volumes, Q 186 times too small, and V_R was 1e-3 m^3; on the gas basis
  that volume gives tau ≈ 0.72 s and X ≈ 0.816.)
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        wgs;
        type        cstr;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( products );

        operation   { V_R 1.0e-2; }   // m^3: tau ≈ 7.2 s on the gas basis
        reaction    wgs_reversible;
    }
);
